    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"5a\"><p><strong>5a</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Region around the peak of the graph is labeled S.</p>\n<p> </p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"5b\"><p><strong>5b</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Neutron</p>\n<p> </p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"5c\"><p><strong>5c</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Reading values from the graph (accept a range of values here)</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"(134 \\times 8.35 + 103 \\times 8.55) - 239 \\times 7.55 \\approx 195\"></span> MeV</p>\n<p>Converting into joules: </p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"(195 \\times 10^{6})(1.6 \\times 10^{-19}) \\approx 3.12 \\times 10^{-11}\"></span> J <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"= 31.2\"></span> pJ</p>\n<p></p></section>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The graph shows how binding energy per nucleon <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{B}\"></span> varies with nucleon number <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"A\"></span>.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>a. Use the letter S to label the region of most stable elements on the graph.</p>\n<p>   [1]</p>\n<p>The following equation shows the fission of plutonium-239.</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"_{\\, \\, \\, 94}^{239}\\textrm{Pu} + X\\rightarrow _{\\, \\, \\, 54}^{134}\\textrm{Xe} + _{\\, \\, \\, 40}^{103}\\textrm{Zr} + 3X\"></span></p>\n<p>b. Write down the name of particle X.</p>\n<p>   [1]</p>\n<p>c. Use the graph to calculate the energy released in this fission reaction. Give your answer in pJ.</p>\n<p>   [3]</p>"
  },
